{
  "action": "After a standard system update you need to restart your session to make\nall the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-28295",
    "CVE-2026-28296"
  ],
  "description": "It was discovered that the GVfs FTP backend incorrectly handled IP\naddresses and ports returned by passive mode responses. A malicious remote\nserver could possibly use this issue to help scan for open ports.\n(CVE-2026-28295)\n\nIt was discovered that the GVfs FTP backend incorrectly handled crafted\nfile paths. A remote attacker could use this issue to terminate or inject\narbitrary FTP commands, or possibly execute arbitrary code.\n(CVE-2026-28296)",
  "id": "USN-8114-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in GVfs.",
